e telling  luffy that he needs to stay calm and  that vivi is strong and competent enough  and can look out for herself reasonable  in air quotes here because while it's  nice that zorro believes in vv i'm not  sure he makes the best argument here for  being honest i mean he reminds luffy  that he trusted in ace to solve his own  problems as well only did zorro somehow  forget how that turned out for him in  the end i mean in case you need a  reminder it's with a fist-sized hole in  the chest and luffy almost losing his  will to live  so  not exactly the best example to bring up  here i feel but i do get the gist of  what he's trying to say since no one  knows where vivi is at the moment  there's really no point in sailing  across the entire grand line looking for  her rightfully so however the rest of  the crew does tease him for it with some  fantastic nicknames including green  kaido and green big mom which were my  two favorites here now interestingly  enough luffy doesn't want to hear any  more news understandably somewhat  because there has been a lot of info  dumb recently however as a result robin  doesn't tell luffy what happened on  amazon lily and that blackbeard has now  taken kobe and i think it's reasonable  to assume that in this case even zorro  might have been willing to go and save  kobe i think it's logical that robin  didn't tell him i mean i don't think she  fully knows just how close kobe zara and  luffy were but yeah it's still  convenient that she doesn't then luffy  shares his actual dream for the very  first time with his crewmates the only  other people he told so far were ace  zabo and shanks but i want to spend too  much time on this topic honestly since  oda sensei is once again only teasing it  here but doesn't reveal anything yet the  reactions of the crew are of course  fantastic and it fits really really well  with what we've already seen from sabo  ace and shanks before i personally felt  that part of luffy's dream was what he  basically already shared with kaido  during the finale of their battle and i  know that there is a theory that luffy  simply wants to throw the world's  biggest party but i think it might still  be something even bigger than that after  all you don't really necessarily have to  become pirate king just for that i know  there's also the idea that he wants to  go to the moon again not exactly pirate  king related at first glance so we'll  just really have to wait and see what it  ends up being point is now his crew  knows and of course karibu who it turns  out has actually been on the ship with  the crew listening in and honestly my  first reaction to this was a bit of  anger i mean you have some of the best  observation hockey users on the planet  on this ship and no one notices him i  mean they did notice him on fishman  island and someone like rayleigh is able  to count the exact number of living  things on an island suddenly karibu can  hide in a barrel completely unnoticed on  open sea but then i remembered that  luffy had actually allowed him to leave  wano on his ship in udon prison so maybe  they all know exactly that he's in there  maybe frankie once again locked him up  there a second time i'm really very  curious to see what oda sensei has in  mind for karibu and who he's working for  blackbeard crocodile someone else maybe  we then skip ahead a couple of days as  the sunny enters the icy and snowy  waters around the next island  i already mentioned that i'm incredibly  excited that we're going to an  unexpected winter island decks though i  don't want to mention here that  apparently we haven't been to a single  autumn island yet in the entire story  kinda sad when you think about it but  winter is awesome too it's my favorite  season now even though the top two  contenders for the next island are off  the table with elbaf and sphynx islands  there are actually two possible winter  islands we know of in the new world that  could be where we're going next the  first one is this mysterious island that  drake went to to get kaido's attention  it's unnamed but everything to be made  out of metal it's also mentioned that  this is an island that apparently was  very important to kaido so it would be a  fitting next destination for the straw  hats after they defeated him i mean it  would surely make for some very  interesting interactions with the people  there that's for sure and in general it  kind of reminded me a lot of karakuri  islands vegapunk's birthplace and where  frankie was sent during the time skip  now on the one piece wiki it says that  this is a winter island located in the  paradise part of the grand line but  looking back through the manga i really  couldn't find anything where i said so  so maybe karakuri island is actually in  the new world that of course could make  it the arc where we finally meet  vegapunk which is really overdue and  then there's also yukiru island which  literally means snow dragon island which  is a winter island somewhere in the new  world where shanks received the news  that whitebeard had torn up his  invitation to meet now if this island is  under shanks's command that would of  course also make for a fantastic next  destination for the crew and a fantastic  lead up to elbaf where i do think luffy  and shanks will finally meet i do hope  that this is going to be maybe a 20 to  40 chapter mini arc similar to zou  before we hopefully do move on to elbaf  and of course we really need to find out  more about emu and their incredible  power i mean there are so many cool  options for an overpowered devil fruit  that they could wield if you're curious  which ones these might be well then make  sure to check out that video right here  or my discussion of the last chapter  here subscribe to the channel yes yo  subscribe  oh view you say hi  say hi
 

